    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:claimant_creditors&amp;rev=1744704736&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-15T08:12:16+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>claimant_creditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:claimant_creditors&amp;rev=1744704736&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Claimants

CLAIMANTS - Creditor claimants are individuals or entities with financial claims against the corporate debtor. They include financial creditors, operational creditors, and secured creditors, each with distinct rights under the IBC framework. Their claims are verified and prioritized during CIRP to ensure equitable distribution of recovered assets.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:committee_creditors&amp;rev=1744704755&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-15T08:12:35+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>committee_creditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:committee_creditors&amp;rev=1744704755&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Committees

CREDITOR COMMITTEES - The Committee of Creditors (CoC) is formed by financial creditors and plays a pivotal role in CIRP. It evaluates resolution plans, monitors the insolvency professional’s actions, and ensures decisions align with value maximization and fairness. The CoC serves as the final authority on accepting or rejecting resolution plans.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:corporate_debtors&amp;rev=1744439873&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-12T06:37:53+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>corporate_debtors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:corporate_debtors&amp;rev=1744439873&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Debtors

CORPORATE DEBTORS - Corporate debtors are entities that have defaulted on their financial obligations, triggering insolvency proceedings under the IBC. They are central to the resolution process, as their assets and operations are managed to maximize value for creditors. During the Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process (CIRP), control shifts from the corporate debtor&#039;s management to insolvency professionals.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:forensic_auditors&amp;rev=1744434440&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-12T05:07:20+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>forensic_auditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:forensic_auditors&amp;rev=1744434440&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Auditors

FORENSIC AUDITORS - Forensic auditors investigate financial irregularities and fraudulent transactions within the corporate debtor’s accounts. Their findings help insolvency professionals and creditor committees identify potential recoverable assets and assess compliance with legal norms.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:insolvency_applicants&amp;rev=1744439840&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-12T06:37:20+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>insolvency_applicants</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:insolvency_applicants&amp;rev=1744439840&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Applicants

IBC APPLICANTS - Insolvency applicants initiate CIRP by filing an application with the National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT). They can be financial creditors, operational creditors, or even corporate debtors themselves seeking resolution of their financial distress.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:insolvency_professionals&amp;rev=1744704787&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-15T08:13:07+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>insolvency_professionals</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:insolvency_professionals&amp;rev=1744704787&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Professionals

INSOLVENCY PROFESSIONALS - Insolvency professionals manage CIRP by taking control of corporate debtor assets, verifying claims, and facilitating resolution plans. They act as intermediaries between stakeholders to ensure compliance with IBC provisions and protect asset value during insolvency proceedings.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:investor_applicants&amp;rev=1744434472&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-12T05:07:52+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>investor_applicants</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:investor_applicants&amp;rev=1744434472&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Investors/Resolution Applicants - Agents

RESOLUTION APPLICANTS - Resolution applicants propose plans for reviving or restructuring the corporate debtor’s operations. Their plans are evaluated by the CoC for feasibility, compliance with legal norms, and alignment with creditor interests.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agents:stakeholder_agents:personal_guarantors&amp;rev=1744434454&amp;do=diff">
